# Configs reference templates

## Template source

`tester-v1/configs/reference/` is canonical. The create-model-configs skill copies from here only; never from `qwen3.5-9b-q8/` or other live model dirs.

## What belongs in reference

- **In reference:** variants that should exist on every model (scaffold + propagate).
- **Not in reference:** model-specific experiments (for example `complex-webapp-build` on one slug only). Do not add those to `reference/` unless the user intends global rollout.

## Promoting and demoting variants

- **Promote to global:** add a variant under `reference/`, then propagate to all models (see [configs-reference-sync.mdc](configs-reference-sync.mdc)).
- **Demote from global:** remove the variant from `reference/` only. Do not delete that variant from live models automatically; model-only copies may remain.

## Editing shared behavior

- **Default:** edit `reference/` first for shared behavior; propagate to models.
- **Exception:** one-off tweaks on a single model stay on that model only and must not be copied into `reference/` unless the user promotes them.

When `reference/` changes, follow [configs-reference-sync.mdc](configs-reference-sync.mdc).

## Do not run on reference

Do not run `single_test_runner.py` or `model_calibration.py` on paths under `configs/reference/`.
